---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<!--
	Variant 4 — "Case Studies"
	Editorial layout: oversized Sinistre display type, numbered project case
	studies told as Context → Built → Outcome. One glyph watermark behind the
	hero is the only runic ornament. The pitch is depth over breadth: three
	stories told properly instead of ten sections.
-->
<BaseLayout
	title="Ahmet Tarik Duyar — Software Engineer"
	description="Case studies in shipping production software: streaming at scale, healthcare education platforms, and systems programming."
	bodyClass="bg-[#0a0b0e] text-gray-200 antialiased"
>
	<main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-10">
		<!-- Hero -->
		<header class="min-h-[80vh] flex flex-col justify-center relative py-20">
			<span class="font-oldturcic absolute right-0 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 text-[16rem] md:text-[22rem] text-blue-400/[0.03] leading-none select-none pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true">𐱅</span>
			<div class="relative">
				<p class="text-sm tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-gray-500 mb-8">Ahmet Tarik Duyar</p>
				<h1 class="font-sinistre text-5xl sm:text-7xl lg:text-8xl text-white leading-[0.95] mb-10">
					Software engineer.<br />
					<span class="text-blue-300">Three stories</span><br />
					about shipping.
				</h1>
				<p class="text-gray-400 max-w-lg leading-relaxed">
					I've spent the last three years building platforms people pay for —
					and keeping them online. Below: what I built, why it was hard, and
					how it turned out.
				</p>
				<div class="flex gap-6 mt-10 text-sm">
					<a href="https://github.com/atduyar" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-gray-500 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">GitHub</a>
					<a href="https://linkedin.com/in/atduyar" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-gray-500 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">LinkedIn</a>
					<a href="mailto:atduyar@gmail.com" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">atduyar@gmail.com</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</header>

		<!-- Case study 01 -->
		<article class="py-20 border-t border-white/10">
			<div class="flex items-baseline gap-6 mb-8">
				<span class="font-sinistre text-5xl text-blue-400/30 select-none">01</span>
				<div>
					<h2 class="font-sinistre text-3xl md:text-4xl text-white">EgeceTV</h2>
					<p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-1">Deniz Egece Co. Ltd. · 2022 — present · Founding engineer</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="md:grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-10 md:pl-[5.5rem]">
				<div class="md:col-span-2 space-y-5 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">The problem.</span> A health and education
						company wanted its video catalog — roughly a thousand titles — available
						on web, iOS, Android, Android TV, and Apple TV, behind a subscription.
						No existing platform, no existing team.
					</p>
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">What I built.</span> The backend from
						scratch: a single GraphQL API serving all five clients, the MySQL
						schema behind it, adaptive bitrate delivery through a CDN, a custom
						CMS for the content team, the subscription payment flow, and the
						CI/CD pipeline that ships it all.
					</p>
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">The outcome.</span> The platform runs in
						production today with over 17,000 paying subscribers. One API, five
						platforms, and a deploy process that doesn't need me in the room.
					</p>
				</div>
				<aside class="mt-8 md:mt-0 text-sm space-y-4">
					<div>
						<p class="text-gray-600 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Scale</p>
						<p class="text-gray-300">17,000+ subscribers<br />~1,000 videos<br />5 client platforms</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<p class="text-gray-600 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Stack</p>
						<p class="text-gray-300">Next.js · GraphQL · MySQL · Prisma · AWS · GitHub Actions</p>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</div>
		</article>

		<!-- Case study 02 -->
		<article class="py-20 border-t border-white/10">
			<div class="flex items-baseline gap-6 mb-8">
				<span class="font-sinistre text-5xl text-blue-400/30 select-none">02</span>
				<div>
					<h2 class="font-sinistre text-3xl md:text-4xl text-white">Distance Education Platform</h2>
					<p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-1">Deniz Egece Co. Ltd. · Team of five</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="md:grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-10 md:pl-[5.5rem]">
				<div class="md:col-span-2 space-y-5 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">The problem.</span> Connect clients with
						psychologists and dietitians remotely — which means live video,
						scheduling across timezones, and health data that genuinely cannot leak.
					</p>
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">What I built.</span> A .NET backend
						structured with Clean Architecture, WebRTC video consultations with
						custom signaling, reservation scheduling, and homework/progress
						tracking between sessions. Encryption at rest and in transit, with
						strict access controls around client records.
					</p>
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">What I learned.</span> Working in a
						five-person team on sensitive data taught me to value boundaries —
						in the architecture and in the database — over speed of first delivery.
					</p>
				</div>
				<aside class="mt-8 md:mt-0 text-sm space-y-4">
					<div>
						<p class="text-gray-600 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Domain</p>
						<p class="text-gray-300">Telehealth · iOS &amp; Android</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<p class="text-gray-600 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Stack</p>
						<p class="text-gray-300">C# / .NET · PostgreSQL · WebRTC · Docker · AWS</p>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</div>
		</article>

		<!-- Case study 03 -->
		<article class="py-20 border-t border-white/10">
			<div class="flex items-baseline gap-6 mb-8">
				<span class="font-sinistre text-5xl text-blue-400/30 select-none">03</span>
				<div>
					<h2 class="font-sinistre text-3xl md:text-4xl text-white">Below the Web Stack</h2>
					<p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-1">Personal work · ongoing</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="md:grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-10 md:pl-[5.5rem]">
				<div class="md:col-span-2 space-y-5 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">Why.</span> Web frameworks hide a lot.
						I want to know what they hide — so I build the layers underneath them
						myself.
					</p>
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">REKV</span> is a type-safe key-value store
						library in Rust: memory-mapped storage, zero-copy deserialization,
						async I/O.
						<a href="https://github.com/atduyar/rekv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">Source ↗</a>
					</p>
					<p>
						<span class="text-gray-200">Make2Game</span> is a 2D game engine
						written from scratch in C++ and OpenGL, with Lua scripting and an
						immediate-mode editor.
						<a href="https://github.com/atduyar/make2game" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">Source ↗</a>
					</p>
					<p>
						Everything I run — including this site — lives on infrastructure I
						administer myself.
					</p>
				</div>
				<aside class="mt-8 md:mt-0 text-sm space-y-4">
					<div>
						<p class="text-gray-600 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Languages</p>
						<p class="text-gray-300">Rust · C · C++ · Lua</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<p class="text-gray-600 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Also</p>
						<p class="text-gray-300">CS honor student,<br />Int'l University of Sarajevo</p>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</div>
		</article>

		<!-- Contact -->
		<footer class="py-24 border-t border-white/10 text-center">
			<h2 class="font-sinistre text-4xl md:text-6xl text-white mb-6">Story four could be yours.</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-400 mb-10">Open to roles and collaborations.</p>
			<a href="mailto:atduyar@gmail.com" class="inline-block px-8 py-4 border border-blue-400/40 text-blue-300 hover:bg-blue-400 hover:text-[#0a0b0e] transition-all duration-300">
				atduyar@gmail.com
			</a>
			<p class="mt-16 text-xs text-gray-600">© 2026 Ahmet Tarik Duyar · Sarajevo</p>
		</footer>
	</main>
</BaseLayout>
